# Terraform IAM Group Cleanup - iamgroup_ammar

This repository contains the Terraform configuration used to manage and clean up temporary AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) resources as part of the Nautilus DevOps environment migration.

## Overview

During the cloud infrastructure migration and optimization phase, temporary resources are occasionally provisioned for one-time testing or operations. This task covers the safe destruction and state management of the `iamgroup_ammar` IAM group (`aws_iam_group.this`) while preserving the underlying infrastructure provisioning code for future deployment.

## Architecture & Resources

* **Terraform Provider:** `aws`
* **Resource Type:** `aws_iam_group`
* **Resource Identifier:** `aws_iam_group.this` (Group Name: `iamgroup_ammar`)

## Repository Structure

```text
├── main.tf                    # Core Terraform configuration defining AWS resources
├── provider.tf                # Provider definitions and region configurations
├── terraform.tfstate          # Local state file tracking managed infrastructure
├── terraform.tfstate.backup   # Previous state backup
└── README.md                  # Project documentation
